insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('76d160d4-954a-531b-ac6c-fff534608db0', 'rg3-comparing-texts-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Rosa and Grandpa Eli$q$, $q$The same author wrote both of these stories about the same two characters.

Text 1: The Bean Seeds

Rosa planted six bean seeds in a pot with Grandpa Eli. Every morning, Rosa checked the pot. Nothing was there but brown dirt. "Why is it taking so long?" Rosa asked. Grandpa Eli smiled. "Seeds work under the soil first. You just cannot see it yet." On the eighth day, a tiny green loop poked up. Rosa clapped. Waiting had been hard, but the sprout was worth it.

Text 2: The Tomato Plant

In summer, Rosa and Grandpa Eli grew a tomato plant in the backyard. The tomatoes stayed small and green for weeks. Rosa wanted to pick one right away. "Not yet," said Grandpa Eli. "Give them time to turn red." Rosa waited and watered the plant each evening. At last, three tomatoes turned bright red. Rosa and Grandpa Eli ate them with a pinch of salt at the picnic table. They were the sweetest tomatoes Rosa had ever tasted.$q$, 'draft')
