insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b68c499e-a8c2-5337-8ea5-d57c0f608cc1', 'rg3-comparing-texts-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Omar and Aunt Lucia$q$, $q$The same author wrote both of these stories about the same two characters.

Text 1: The Blank Wall

The wall beside the Maple Street Community Center was plain and gray. Aunt Lucia was an artist, and she had an idea. "Let's paint a mural," she told her nephew, Omar. Omar sketched birds, trees and a big yellow sun. On Saturday, neighbors came with brushes. Mr. Kim painted the trees. The Ortiz twins painted the birds. Omar and Aunt Lucia painted the sun together. By evening, the gray wall was full of color.

Text 2: The Rainy Week

A week later, a hard rain poured down on Maple Street. Omar worried about the mural. Would the colors wash away? Aunt Lucia and Omar hurried outside with umbrellas. Some paint near the bottom had dripped. Omar felt like crying. "We can fix it," Aunt Lucia said. On the next sunny day, the neighbors came back with brushes. This time, they also added a clear coat to protect the paint. Omar stepped back and smiled. The mural looked even better than before.$q$, 'draft')
