insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b9ef8a17-33b1-587c-bfab-4c7145df1aa2', 'rg3-comparing-texts-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Kenji and Grandma Ruth$q$, $q$The same author wrote a story and a poem about the same two characters.

Text 1: The Museum Visit

Kenji and Grandma Ruth visited the Pine Hill Town Museum. In one room stood a shiny brass bell. A sign said it came from the town's first school. Grandma Ruth smiled. "I rang that bell when I was your age," she said. Long ago, the school had only one room. Children of all ages learned together. Each morning, one student rang the bell to start the day. Kenji touched the cool metal. Now the old bell felt like part of the family story.

Text 2: Grandma's Bell

When Grandma Ruth was small and quick,
She pulled the rope, a happy trick.
Ding, dong, the bell would say,
Come inside to learn today!

Now it rests where people see,
A piece of then for you and me.
Kenji listens, close and near,
To stories from another year.$q$, 'draft')
