-- Passage rg3-comparing-texts-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('3ed0048b-2207-5b0b-bddb-dab91171dbd9', 'rg3-comparing-texts-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Nia and Uncle Theo$q$, $q$The same author wrote both of these stories about the same two characters.

Text 1: The Moon Journal

Nia wanted to know why the moon looked different every night. Uncle Theo gave Nia a notebook. "Look each night and draw what you see," he said. So Nia did. Some nights the moon was a thin curve. Other nights it was half a circle. After about four weeks, the pages showed the moon growing and shrinking in a pattern. Nia ran to show Uncle Theo. "It repeats!" Nia said. Watching carefully had answered the question.

Text 2: Night on the Hill

One summer night, Uncle Theo drove Nia to a dark hill outside town. They spread a blanket on the grass. "Tonight there may be shooting stars," Uncle Theo said. At first, Nia saw nothing but still stars. Nia wanted to go home. Uncle Theo said, "Keep watching." Then a bright streak zipped across the sky. Then another! Nia counted eleven by midnight. On the drive home, Nia wrote every one in the moon journal.$q$, 'draft')
