-- Passage rg3-comparing-texts-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('33d00f72-db8d-5996-ba6f-2938697b987d', 'rg3-comparing-texts-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Leo and Amara$q$, $q$The same author wrote a story and a poem about the same two characters.

Text 1: The Snow Day

Leo and Amara are brother and sister, and Amara is the younger one. One morning, school was closed because of snow. Leo and Amara pulled on boots and mittens. They wanted to build the biggest snowman on the block. Leo rolled a huge ball for the bottom. Amara rolled the middle. But the head kept falling off. Amara had an idea. "Let's pack it with more snow, like glue." It worked! The snowman stood tall with a carrot nose. Leo gave Amara a high five.

Text 2: My Brother and Me

I'm Amara, small but bright,
My brother Leo rolls with might.
The head fell down, plop, plop, plop,
I packed the snow to make it stop.

Now our snowman stands up tall,
The best one on the block of all.
Leo says, "Great job, little one!"
And we both laugh out in the sun.$q$, 'draft')
