        '3-5', $q$Zara and Tomas$q$, $q$The same author wrote both of these stories about the same two characters.

Text 1: The Lemonade Stand

Zara and Tomas wanted to help the Riverside Animal Shelter. The shelter needed money for dog food. So the two friends set up a lemonade stand in Zara's front yard. For the first hour, only one person stopped. Tomas frowned. "Maybe people cannot see us," Zara said. They made a big sign that said, "Lemonade for Shelter Pets!" Soon a line of neighbors formed. By the end of the day, they had earned forty dollars.

Text 2: The Shelter Visit

On Monday, Zara and Tomas carried a jar of money to the Riverside Animal Shelter. The worker at the desk counted it and grinned. "This will buy food for a whole month!" A shy brown puppy peeked out from a crate. Tomas knelt down and held out a hand. The puppy sniffed, then licked Tomas's fingers. Zara laughed. Walking home, the friends were already planning their next stand. Helping felt too good to stop.$q$, 'draft')
