-- Passage rg3-connections-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b4f751f4-5862-5099-930e-b12c9155778d', 'rg3-connections-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-connections'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Library on Wheels$q$, $q$About one hundred years ago, Clover County had only one library. It was in the biggest town. Many families lived on farms far away. The roads were bumpy dirt paths, and few people had cars. As a result, most farm children almost never got to borrow a book.

A librarian named Tomas Reyes wanted to solve this problem. Tomas had an idea. If the children could not come to the library, the library could go to the children.

First, Tomas got an old wagon and a horse. Next, volunteers built wooden shelves inside the wagon. Then they filled the shelves with picture books, storybooks and books about farming. Every Saturday, Tomas drove the wagon along the country roads. The wagon stopped at farms and at small schools.

The children were thrilled. They chose books and returned them the next week. Because they could read more often, many children became stronger readers. Parents borrowed books about growing crops, and some farms grew more food.

The wagon became so popular that it could not hold enough books. A few years later, the county bought a truck. The truck could carry three times as many books and travel farther in one day. Soon it was visiting every corner of Clover County.

Today, many towns still have library buses that bring books to people who live far away.$q$, 'draft')
