-- Passage rg3-literary-structure-pov-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('25adaad8-da1f-55ae-b51c-53f6f87285fb', 'rg3-literary-structure-pov-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Cardboard Robot$q$, $q$Chapter 1: Too Many Helpers

I had one week to build a robot for the school art show. My plan was simple. I would use three boxes, gray paint, and nothing else. A real robot looks clean and plain.

My little brother Mateo did not agree. He glued bottle caps on the chest for buttons. He taped a foil cupcake liner on top for an antenna. He drew a big smile on the face with a red marker.

"Stop it!" I said. "You are ruining everything." I was so upset that I almost painted over the smile.

Chapter 2: The Art Show

On Friday the gym was full of art. My robot stood near the door, smile and all. I wanted to hide behind it.

Then a group of kindergartners ran over. They pressed every bottle cap button and made beeping sounds. A teacher pointed at the foil antenna and laughed. "This robot looks so friendly," she said.

By the end of the night, people had left more happy notes on our robot than on any other project. I looked at Mateo. "Our robot," I said. "Thanks for the buttons."$q$, 'draft')
